---The crop properties of an object enclosed in a container. For example, an Image. The crop properties is represented by the offsets of four edges which define a crop rectangle. The offsets are measured in percentage from the corresponding edges of the object's original bounding rectangle towards inside, relative to the object's original dimensions. - If the offset is in the interval (0, 1), the corresponding edge of crop rectangle is positioned inside of the object's original bounding rectangle. - If the offset is negative or greater than 1, the corresponding edge of crop rectangle is positioned outside of the object's original bounding rectangle. - If the left edge of the crop rectangle is on the right side of its right edge, the object will be flipped horizontally. - If the top edge of the crop rectangle is below its bottom edge, the object will be flipped vertically. - If all offsets and rotation angle is 0, the object is not cropped. After cropping, the content in the crop rectangle will be stretched to fit its container.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.CropProperties
---@field angle? number The rotation angle of the crop window around its center, in radians. Rotation angle is applied after the offset.
---@field bottomOffset? number The offset specifies the bottom edge of the crop rectangle that is located above the original bounding rectangle bottom edge, relative to the object's original height.
---@field rightOffset? number The offset specifies the right edge of the crop rectangle that is located to the left of the original bounding rectangle right edge, relative to the object's original width.
---@field topOffset? number The offset specifies the top edge of the crop rectangle that is located below the original bounding rectangle top edge, relative to the object's original height.
---@field leftOffset? number The offset specifies the left edge of the crop rectangle that is located to the right of the original bounding rectangle left edge, relative to the object's original width.

---Deletes a reply Post from a CommentThread. Returns a 400 bad request error if: - The requesting user is not the author of the post. - The reply post contains a comment action. - The reply post contains an assignee.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.DeleteCommentReplyRequest
---@field postId? string The ID of the reply Post being deleted.
---@field commentId? string The ID of the CommentThread which the post belongs to.

---Deletes a CommentThread. Returns a 400 bad request error if the requesting user is not the author of the headPost.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.DeleteCommentRequest
---@field commentId? string The ID of the CommentThread that is being deleted.

---Deletes an object, either pages or page elements, from the presentation.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.DeleteObjectRequest
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the page or page element to delete. If after a delete operation a group contains only 1 or no page elements, the group is also deleted. If a placeholder is deleted on a layout, any empty inheriting placeholders are also deleted.

---Deletes bullets from all of the paragraphs that overlap with the given text index range. The nesting level of each paragraph will be visually preserved by adding indent to the start of the corresponding paragraph.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.DeleteParagraphBulletsRequest
---@field cellLocation? gcp.slides_v1.TableCellLocation The optional table cell location if the text to be modified is in a table cell. If present, the object_id must refer to a table.
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the shape or table containing the text to delete bullets from.
---@field textRange? gcp.slides_v1.Range The range of text to delete bullets from, based on TextElement indexes.

---Deletes a column from a table.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.DeleteTableColumnRequest
---@field cellLocation? gcp.slides_v1.TableCellLocation The reference table cell location from which a column will be deleted. The column this cell spans will be deleted. If this is a merged cell, multiple columns will be deleted. If no columns remain in the table after this deletion, the whole table is deleted.
---@field tableObjectId? string The table to delete columns from.

---Deletes a row from a table.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.DeleteTableRowRequest
---@field tableObjectId? string The table to delete rows from.
---@field cellLocation? gcp.slides_v1.TableCellLocation The reference table cell location from which a row will be deleted. The row this cell spans will be deleted. If this is a merged cell, multiple rows will be deleted. If no rows remain in the table after this deletion, the whole table is deleted.

---Deletes text from a shape or a table cell.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.DeleteTextRequest
---@field textRange? gcp.slides_v1.Range The range of text to delete, based on TextElement indexes. There is always an implicit newline character at the end of a shape's or table cell's text that cannot be deleted. `Range.Type.ALL` will use the correct bounds, but care must be taken when specifying explicit bounds for range types `FROM_START_INDEX` and `FIXED_RANGE`. For example, if the text is "ABC", followed by an implicit newline, then the maximum value is 2 for `text_range.start_index` and 3 for `text_range.end_index`. Deleting text that crosses a paragraph boundary may result in changes to paragraph styles and lists as the two paragraphs are merged. Ranges that include only one code unit of a surrogate pair are expanded to include both code units.
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the shape or table from which the text will be deleted.
---@field cellLocation? gcp.slides_v1.TableCellLocation The optional table cell location if the text is to be deleted from a table cell. If present, the object_id must refer to a table.

---A magnitude in a single direction in the specified units.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.Dimension
---@field magnitude? number The magnitude.
---@field unit? gcp.slides_v1.DimensionUnitEnum|string The units for magnitude.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.DimensionUnitEnum "UNIT_UNSPECIFIED"|"EMU"|"PT"

---Duplicates a slide or page element. When duplicating a slide, the duplicate slide will be created immediately following the specified slide. When duplicating a page element, the duplicate will be placed on the same page at the same position as the original.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.DuplicateObjectRequest
---@field objectId? string The ID of the object to duplicate.
---@field objectIds? gcp.slides_v1.StringMap The object being duplicated may contain other objects, for example when duplicating a slide or a group page element. This map defines how the IDs of duplicated objects are generated: the keys are the IDs of the original objects and its values are the IDs that will be assigned to the corresponding duplicate object. The ID of the source object's duplicate may be specified in this map as well, using the same value of the `object_id` field as a key and the newly desired ID as the value. All keys must correspond to existing IDs in the presentation. All values must be unique in the presentation and must start with an alphanumeric character or an underscore (matches regex `[a-zA-Z0-9_]`); remaining characters may include those as well as a hyphen or colon (matches regex `[a-zA-Z0-9_-:]`). The length of the new ID must not be less than 5 or greater than 50. If any IDs of source objects are omitted from the map, a new random ID will be assigned. If the map is empty or unset, all duplicate objects will receive a new random ID.

---The response of duplicating an object.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.DuplicateObjectResponse
---@field objectId? string The ID of the new duplicate object.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.GetPresentationsCommentsViewModeEnum "COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_DEFAULT_FOR_CURRENT_ACCESS"|"COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_OMITTED"|"COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_INCLUDED"

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.GetPresentationsPagesCommentsViewModeEnum "COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_DEFAULT_FOR_CURRENT_ACCESS"|"COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_OMITTED"|"COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_INCLUDED"

---@class gcp.slides_v1.GetPresentationsPagesRequest
---@field presentationId string The ID of the presentation to retrieve.
---@field pageObjectId string The object ID of the page to retrieve.
---@field commentsViewMode? gcp.slides_v1.GetPresentationsPagesCommentsViewModeEnum|string The comments view mode to apply to the page. This allows viewing the page with comments omitted or included. If one is not specified, COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_OMITTED is used.

---@class gcp.slides_v1.GetPresentationsRequest
---@field presentationId string The ID of the presentation to retrieve.
---@field commentsViewMode? gcp.slides_v1.GetPresentationsCommentsViewModeEnum|string The comments view mode to apply to the presentation. This allows viewing the presentation with comments omitted or included. If one is not specified, COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_OMITTED is used.

---@class gcp.slides_v1.GetThumbnailPresentationsPagesRequest
---@field presentationId string The ID of the presentation to retrieve.
---@field ["thumbnailProperties.thumbnailSize"]? gcp.slides_v1.GetThumbnailPresentationsPagesThumbnailProperties_thumbnailSizeEnum|string The optional thumbnail image size. If you don't specify the size, the server chooses a default size of the image.
---@field ["thumbnailProperties.mimeType"]? gcp.slides_v1.GetThumbnailPresentationsPagesThumbnailProperties_mimeTypeEnum|string The optional mime type of the thumbnail image. If you don't specify the mime type, the mime type defaults to PNG.
---@field pageObjectId string The object ID of the page whose thumbnail to retrieve.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.GetThumbnailPresentationsPagesThumbnailProperties_mimeTypeEnum "PNG"

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.GetThumbnailPresentationsPagesThumbnailProperties_thumbnailSizeEnum "THUMBNAIL_SIZE_UNSPECIFIED"|"LARGE"|"MEDIUM"|"SMALL"|"WIDTH2000_PX"

---A PageElement kind representing a joined collection of PageElements.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.Group
---@field children? gcp.slides_v1.PageElementList The collection of elements in the group. The minimum size of a group is 2.

---Groups objects to create an object group. For example, groups PageElements to create a Group on the same page as all the children.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.GroupObjectsRequest
---@field childrenObjectIds? gcp.slides_v1.StringList The object IDs of the objects to group. Only page elements can be grouped. There should be at least two page elements on the same page that are not already in another group. Some page elements, such as videos, tables and placeholders cannot be grouped.
---@field groupObjectId? string A user-supplied object ID for the group to be created. If you specify an ID, it must be unique among all pages and page elements in the presentation. The ID must start with an alphanumeric character or an underscore (matches regex `[a-zA-Z0-9_]`); remaining characters may include those as well as a hyphen or colon (matches regex `[a-zA-Z0-9_-:]`). The length of the ID must not be less than 5 or greater than 50. If you don't specify an ID, a unique one is generated.

---The result of grouping objects.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.GroupObjectsResponse
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the created group.

---A PageElement kind representing an image.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.Image
---@field imageProperties? gcp.slides_v1.ImageProperties The properties of the image.
---@field placeholder? gcp.slides_v1.Placeholder Placeholders are page elements that inherit from corresponding placeholders on layouts and masters. If set, the image is a placeholder image and any inherited properties can be resolved by looking at the parent placeholder identified by the Placeholder.parent_object_id field.
---@field contentUrl? string An URL to an image with a default lifetime of 30 minutes. This URL is tagged with the account of the requester. Anyone with the URL effectively accesses the image as the original requester. Access to the image may be lost if the presentation's sharing settings change.
---@field sourceUrl? string The source URL is the URL used to insert the image. The source URL can be empty.

---The properties of the Image.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.ImageProperties
---@field link? gcp.slides_v1.Link The hyperlink destination of the image. If unset, there is no link.
---@field shadow? gcp.slides_v1.Shadow The shadow of the image. If not set, the image has no shadow. This property is read-only.
---@field brightness? number The brightness effect of the image. The value should be in the interval [-1.0, 1.0], where 0 means no effect. This property is read-only.
---@field recolor? gcp.slides_v1.Recolor The recolor effect of the image. If not set, the image is not recolored. This property is read-only.
---@field outline? gcp.slides_v1.Outline The outline of the image. If not set, the image has no outline.
---@field contrast? number The contrast effect of the image. The value should be in the interval [-1.0, 1.0], where 0 means no effect. This property is read-only.
---@field transparency? number The transparency effect of the image. The value should be in the interval [0.0, 1.0], where 0 means no effect and 1 means completely transparent. This property is read-only.
---@field cropProperties? gcp.slides_v1.CropProperties The crop properties of the image. If not set, the image is not cropped. This property is read-only.

---Inserts a CommentThread into the presentation.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.InsertCommentRequest
---@field assigneeEmailAddress? string Optional. The email address of the assignee of the comment. Leave empty for a non-assigned comment. May not exceed 2048 UTF-8 code units.
---@field tableCellTextAnchor? gcp.slides_v1.TableCellTextAnchor Anchors a comment to a specific range of text within a single cell in a Table.
---@field content? string The text of the comment, as plain text. This text content will be handled similarly to comments created in the Slides editor. It will have similar behaviors for formatting, notifications, etc. This field cannot be empty, and must not exceed 2048 UTF-8 code units.
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the Page or PageElement that is tied to this comment. If the specified object_id is a Group, the comment will be anchored to at most 100 of the group's non-group descendants.
---@field shapeTextAnchor? gcp.slides_v1.ShapeTextAnchor Anchors a comment to a specific range of text within a Shape.
---@field tableAnchor? gcp.slides_v1.TableAnchor Anchors a comment to a specific range of cells within a Table. Returns a 400 bad request error if no cells within the range contain text.

---The result of creating a comment.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.InsertCommentResponse
---@field commentThread? gcp.slides_v1.CommentThread The newly-inserted comment thread.

---Inserts columns into a table. Other columns in the table will be resized to fit the new column.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.InsertTableColumnsRequest
---@field number? number The number of columns to be inserted. Maximum 20 per request.
---@field tableObjectId? string The table to insert columns into.
---@field insertRight? boolean Whether to insert new columns to the right of the reference cell location. - `True`: insert to the right. - `False`: insert to the left.
---@field cellLocation? gcp.slides_v1.TableCellLocation The reference table cell location from which columns will be inserted. A new column will be inserted to the left (or right) of the column where the reference cell is. If the reference cell is a merged cell, a new column will be inserted to the left (or right) of the merged cell.

---Inserts rows into a table.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.InsertTableRowsRequest
---@field tableObjectId? string The table to insert rows into.
---@field number? number The number of rows to be inserted. Maximum 20 per request.
---@field insertBelow? boolean Whether to insert new rows below the reference cell location. - `True`: insert below the cell. - `False`: insert above the cell.
---@field cellLocation? gcp.slides_v1.TableCellLocation The reference table cell location from which rows will be inserted. A new row will be inserted above (or below) the row where the reference cell is. If the reference cell is a merged cell, a new row will be inserted above (or below) the merged cell.

---Inserts text into a shape or a table cell.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.InsertTextRequest
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the shape or table where the text will be inserted.
---@field cellLocation? gcp.slides_v1.TableCellLocation The optional table cell location if the text is to be inserted into a table cell. If present, the object_id must refer to a table.
---@field text? string The text to be inserted. Inserting a newline character will implicitly create a new ParagraphMarker at that index. The paragraph style of the new paragraph will be copied from the paragraph at the current insertion index, including lists and bullets. Text styles for inserted text will be determined automatically, generally preserving the styling of neighboring text. In most cases, the text will be added to the TextRun that exists at the insertion index. Some control characters (U+0000-U+0008, U+000C-U+001F) and characters from the Unicode Basic Multilingual Plane Private Use Area (U+E000-U+F8FF) will be stripped out of the inserted text.
---@field insertionIndex? number The index where the text will be inserted, in Unicode code units, based on TextElement indexes. The index is zero-based and is computed from the start of the string. The index may be adjusted to prevent insertions inside Unicode grapheme clusters. In these cases, the text will be inserted immediately after the grapheme cluster.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.IntegerList number[]

---The user-specified ID mapping for a placeholder that will be created on a slide from a specified layout.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.LayoutPlaceholderIdMapping
---@field layoutPlaceholder? gcp.slides_v1.Placeholder The placeholder on a layout that will be applied to a slide. Only type and index are needed. For example, a predefined `TITLE_AND_BODY` layout may usually have a TITLE placeholder with index 0 and a BODY placeholder with index 0.
---@field layoutPlaceholderObjectId? string The object ID of the placeholder on a layout that will be applied to a slide.
---@field objectId? string A user-supplied object ID for the placeholder identified above that to be created onto a slide. If you specify an ID, it must be unique among all pages and page elements in the presentation. The ID must start with an alphanumeric character or an underscore (matches regex `[a-zA-Z0-9_]`); remaining characters may include those as well as a hyphen or colon (matches regex `[a-zA-Z0-9_-:]`). The length of the ID must not be less than 5 or greater than 50. If you don't specify an ID, a unique one is generated.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.LayoutPlaceholderIdMappingList gcp.slides_v1.LayoutPlaceholderIdMapping[]

---The properties of Page are only relevant for pages with page_type LAYOUT.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.LayoutProperties
---@field masterObjectId? string The object ID of the master that this layout is based on.
---@field displayName? string The human-readable name of the layout.
---@field name? string The name of the layout.

---Slide layout reference. This may reference either: - A predefined layout - One of the layouts in the presentation.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.LayoutReference
---@field layoutId? string Layout ID: the object ID of one of the layouts in the presentation.
---@field predefinedLayout? gcp.slides_v1.LayoutReferencePredefinedLayoutEnum|string Predefined layout.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.LayoutReferencePredefinedLayoutEnum "PREDEFINED_LAYOUT_UNSPECIFIED"|"BLANK"|"CAPTION_ONLY"|"TITLE"|"TITLE_AND_BODY"|"TITLE_AND_TWO_COLUMNS"|"TITLE_ONLY"|"SECTION_HEADER"|"SECTION_TITLE_AND_DESCRIPTION"|"ONE_COLUMN_TEXT"|"MAIN_POINT"|"BIG_NUMBER"

---A PageElement kind representing a non-connector line, straight connector, curved connector, or bent connector.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.Line
---@field lineCategory? gcp.slides_v1.LineLineCategoryEnum|string The category of the line. It matches the `category` specified in CreateLineRequest, and can be updated with UpdateLineCategoryRequest.
---@field lineProperties? gcp.slides_v1.LineProperties The properties of the line.
---@field lineType? gcp.slides_v1.LineLineTypeEnum|string The type of the line.

---The properties for one end of a Line connection.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.LineConnection
---@field connectionSiteIndex? number The index of the connection site on the connected page element. In most cases, it corresponds to the predefined connection site index from the ECMA-376 standard. More information on those connection sites can be found in both the description of the "cxn" attribute in section 20.1.9.9 and "Annex H. Example Predefined DrawingML Shape and Text Geometries" of "Office Open XML File Formats - Fundamentals and Markup Language Reference", part 1 of [ECMA-376 5th edition](https://ecma-international.org/publications-and-standards/standards/ecma-376/). The position of each connection site can also be viewed from Slides editor.
---@field connectedObjectId? string The object ID of the connected page element. Some page elements, such as groups, tables, and lines do not have connection sites and therefore cannot be connected to a connector line.

---The fill of the line.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.LineFill
---@field solidFill? gcp.slides_v1.SolidFill Solid color fill.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.LineLineCategoryEnum "LINE_CATEGORY_UNSPECIFIED"|"STRAIGHT"|"BENT"|"CURVED"

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.LineLineTypeEnum "TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"STRAIGHT_CONNECTOR_1"|"BENT_CONNECTOR_2"|"BENT_CONNECTOR_3"|"BENT_CONNECTOR_4"|"BENT_CONNECTOR_5"|"CURVED_CONNECTOR_2"|"CURVED_CONNECTOR_3"|"CURVED_CONNECTOR_4"|"CURVED_CONNECTOR_5"|"STRAIGHT_LINE"

---The properties of the Line. When unset, these fields default to values that match the appearance of new lines created in the Slides editor.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.LineProperties
---@field dashStyle? gcp.slides_v1.LinePropertiesDashStyleEnum|string The dash style of the line.
---@field endArrow? gcp.slides_v1.LinePropertiesEndArrowEnum|string The style of the arrow at the end of the line.
---@field startConnection? gcp.slides_v1.LineConnection The connection at the beginning of the line. If unset, there is no connection. Only lines with a Type indicating it is a "connector" can have a `start_connection`.
---@field startArrow? gcp.slides_v1.LinePropertiesStartArrowEnum|string The style of the arrow at the beginning of the line.
---@field link? gcp.slides_v1.Link The hyperlink destination of the line. If unset, there is no link.
---@field lineFill? gcp.slides_v1.LineFill The fill of the line. The default line fill matches the defaults for new lines created in the Slides editor.
---@field weight? gcp.slides_v1.Dimension The thickness of the line.
---@field endConnection? gcp.slides_v1.LineConnection The connection at the end of the line. If unset, there is no connection. Only lines with a Type indicating it is a "connector" can have an `end_connection`.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.LinePropertiesDashStyleEnum "DASH_STYLE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SOLID"|"DOT"|"DASH"|"DASH_DOT"|"LONG_DASH"|"LONG_DASH_DOT"

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.LinePropertiesEndArrowEnum "ARROW_STYLE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NONE"|"STEALTH_ARROW"|"FILL_ARROW"|"FILL_CIRCLE"|"FILL_SQUARE"|"FILL_DIAMOND"|"OPEN_ARROW"|"OPEN_CIRCLE"|"OPEN_SQUARE"|"OPEN_DIAMOND"

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.LinePropertiesStartArrowEnum "ARROW_STYLE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NONE"|"STEALTH_ARROW"|"FILL_ARROW"|"FILL_CIRCLE"|"FILL_SQUARE"|"FILL_DIAMOND"|"OPEN_ARROW"|"OPEN_CIRCLE"|"OPEN_SQUARE"|"OPEN_DIAMOND"

---A hypertext link.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.Link
