---@field nestingLevel? gcp.slides_v1.NestingLevelMap A map of nesting levels to the properties of bullets at the associated level. A list has at most nine levels of nesting, so the possible values for the keys of this map are 0 through 8, inclusive.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.ListMap { [string]: gcp.slides_v1.List }

---The properties of Page that are only relevant for pages with page_type MASTER.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.MasterProperties
---@field displayName? string The human-readable name of the master.

---Merges cells in a Table.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.MergeTableCellsRequest
---@field tableRange? gcp.slides_v1.TableRange The table range specifying which cells of the table to merge. Any text in the cells being merged will be concatenated and stored in the upper-left ("head") cell of the range. If the range is non-rectangular (which can occur in some cases where the range covers cells that are already merged), a 400 bad request error is returned.
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the table.

---Contains properties describing the look and feel of a list bullet at a given level of nesting.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.NestingLevel
---@field bulletStyle? gcp.slides_v1.TextStyle The style of a bullet at this level of nesting.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.NestingLevelMap { [string]: gcp.slides_v1.NestingLevel }

---The properties of Page that are only relevant for pages with page_type NOTES.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.NotesProperties
---@field speakerNotesObjectId? string The object ID of the shape on this notes page that contains the speaker notes for the corresponding slide. The actual shape may not always exist on the notes page. Inserting text using this object ID will automatically create the shape. In this case, the actual shape may have different object ID. The `GetPresentation` or `GetPage` action will always return the latest object ID.

---Represents comment anchor data tied to a Slides object, for example a `Page` or PageElement.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.ObjectAnchor
---@field tableCellAnchors? gcp.slides_v1.TableCellAnchors Populated for Tables that have comments anchored to ranges of text in one or more of the table's cells.
---@field shapeTextAnchors? gcp.slides_v1.ShapeTextAnchors Populated for Shapes that have comments anchored to ranges of text in the shape's text.
---@field objectId? string Output only. The page or page element that the comment thread is anchored to.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.ObjectAnchorList gcp.slides_v1.ObjectAnchor[]

---A themeable solid color value.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.OpaqueColor
---@field rgbColor? gcp.slides_v1.RgbColor An opaque RGB color.
---@field themeColor? gcp.slides_v1.OpaqueColorThemeColorEnum|string An opaque theme color.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.OpaqueColorThemeColorEnum "THEME_COLOR_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"DARK1"|"LIGHT1"|"DARK2"|"LIGHT2"|"ACCENT1"|"ACCENT2"|"ACCENT3"|"ACCENT4"|"ACCENT5"|"ACCENT6"|"HYPERLINK"|"FOLLOWED_HYPERLINK"|"TEXT1"|"BACKGROUND1"|"TEXT2"|"BACKGROUND2"

---A color that can either be fully opaque or fully transparent.
