---The outline of a PageElement. If these fields are unset, they may be inherited from a parent placeholder if it exists. If there is no parent, the fields will default to the value used for new page elements created in the Slides editor, which may depend on the page element kind.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.Outline
---@field outlineFill? gcp.slides_v1.OutlineFill The fill of the outline.
---@field propertyState? gcp.slides_v1.OutlinePropertyStateEnum|string The outline property state. Updating the outline on a page element will implicitly update this field to `RENDERED`, unless another value is specified in the same request. To have no outline on a page element, set this field to `NOT_RENDERED`. In this case, any other outline fields set in the same request will be ignored.
---@field dashStyle? gcp.slides_v1.OutlineDashStyleEnum|string The dash style of the outline.
---@field weight? gcp.slides_v1.Dimension The thickness of the outline.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.OutlineDashStyleEnum "DASH_STYLE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SOLID"|"DOT"|"DASH"|"DASH_DOT"|"LONG_DASH"|"LONG_DASH_DOT"

---The fill of the outline.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.OutlineFill
---@field solidFill? gcp.slides_v1.SolidFill Solid color fill.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.OutlinePropertyStateEnum "RENDERED"|"NOT_RENDERED"|"INHERIT"

---A page in a presentation.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.Page
---@field revisionId? string Output only. The revision ID of the presentation. Can be used in update requests to assert the presentation revision hasn't changed since the last read operation. Only populated if the user has edit access to the presentation. The revision ID is not a sequential number but an opaque string. The format of the revision ID might change over time. A returned revision ID is only guaranteed to be valid for 24 hours after it has been returned and cannot be shared across users. If the revision ID is unchanged between calls, then the presentation has not changed. Conversely, a changed ID (for the same presentation and user) usually means the presentation has been updated. However, a changed ID can also be due to internal factors such as ID format changes.
---@field pageElements? gcp.slides_v1.PageElementList The page elements rendered on the page.
---@field pageType? gcp.slides_v1.PagePageTypeEnum|string The type of the page.
---@field slideProperties? gcp.slides_v1.SlideProperties Slide specific properties. Only set if page_type = SLIDE.
---@field masterProperties? gcp.slides_v1.MasterProperties Master specific properties. Only set if page_type = MASTER.
---@field commentsViewMode? gcp.slides_v1.PageCommentsViewModeEnum|string Output only. The comments view mode applied to the page. Only populated if the page was fetched via a GetPageRequest with a populated comments_view_mode.
---@field objectId? string The object ID for this page. Object IDs used by Page and PageElement share the same namespace.
---@field notesProperties? gcp.slides_v1.NotesProperties Notes specific properties. Only set if page_type = NOTES.
---@field pageProperties? gcp.slides_v1.PageProperties The properties of the page.
---@field commentAnchors? gcp.slides_v1.CommentAnchorList Output only. The comment anchors present on the page.
---@field comments? gcp.slides_v1.CommentThreadList Output only. The comment threads associated with the page. Only populated if the page was fetched via a GetPageRequest with a populated comments_view_mode. Otherwise, comments are returned in the Presentation via the GetPresentationRequest.
---@field layoutProperties? gcp.slides_v1.LayoutProperties Layout specific properties. Only set if page_type = LAYOUT.

---The page background fill.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.PageBackgroundFill
---@field stretchedPictureFill? gcp.slides_v1.StretchedPictureFill Stretched picture fill.
---@field solidFill? gcp.slides_v1.SolidFill Solid color fill.
---@field propertyState? gcp.slides_v1.PageBackgroundFillPropertyStateEnum|string The background fill property state. Updating the fill on a page will implicitly update this field to `RENDERED`, unless another value is specified in the same request. To have no fill on a page, set this field to `NOT_RENDERED`. In this case, any other fill fields set in the same request will be ignored.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.PageBackgroundFillPropertyStateEnum "RENDERED"|"NOT_RENDERED"|"INHERIT"

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.PageCommentsViewModeEnum "COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_DEFAULT_FOR_CURRENT_ACCESS"|"COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_OMITTED"|"COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_INCLUDED"

---A visual element rendered on a page.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.PageElement
---@field size? gcp.slides_v1.Size The size of the page element.
---@field objectId? string The object ID for this page element. Object IDs used by google.apps.slides.v1.Page and google.apps.slides.v1.PageElement share the same namespace.
---@field table? gcp.slides_v1.Table A table page element.
---@field elementGroup? gcp.slides_v1.Group A collection of page elements joined as a single unit.
---@field transform? gcp.slides_v1.AffineTransform The transform of the page element. The visual appearance of the page element is determined by its absolute transform. To compute the absolute transform, preconcatenate a page element's transform with the transforms of all of its parent groups. If the page element is not in a group, its absolute transform is the same as the value in this field. The initial transform for the newly created Group is always the identity transform.
---@field wordArt? gcp.slides_v1.WordArt A word art page element.
---@field sheetsChart? gcp.slides_v1.SheetsChart A linked chart embedded from Google Sheets. Unlinked charts are represented as images.
---@field speakerSpotlight? gcp.slides_v1.SpeakerSpotlight A Speaker Spotlight.
---@field description? string The description of the page element. Combined with title to display alt text. The field is not supported for Group elements.
---@field image? gcp.slides_v1.Image An image page element.
---@field title? string The title of the page element. Combined with description to display alt text. The field is not supported for Group elements.
---@field video? gcp.slides_v1.Video A video page element.
---@field shape? gcp.slides_v1.Shape A generic shape.
---@field line? gcp.slides_v1.Line A line page element.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.PageElementList gcp.slides_v1.PageElement[]

---Common properties for a page element. Note: When you initially create a PageElement, the API may modify the values of both `size` and `transform`, but the visual size will be unchanged.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.PageElementProperties
---@field size? gcp.slides_v1.Size The size of the element.
---@field pageObjectId? string The object ID of the page where the element is located.
---@field transform? gcp.slides_v1.AffineTransform The transform for the element.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.PageList gcp.slides_v1.Page[]

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.PagePageTypeEnum "SLIDE"|"MASTER"|"LAYOUT"|"NOTES"|"NOTES_MASTER"

---The properties of the Page. The page will inherit properties from the parent page. Depending on the page type the hierarchy is defined in either SlideProperties or LayoutProperties.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.PageProperties
---@field pageBackgroundFill? gcp.slides_v1.PageBackgroundFill The background fill of the page. If unset, the background fill is inherited from a parent page if it exists. If the page has no parent, then the background fill defaults to the corresponding fill in the Slides editor.
---@field colorScheme? gcp.slides_v1.ColorScheme The color scheme of the page. If unset, the color scheme is inherited from a parent page. If the page has no parent, the color scheme uses a default Slides color scheme, matching the defaults in the Slides editor. Only the concrete colors of the first 12 ThemeColorTypes are editable. In addition, only the color scheme on `Master` pages can be updated. To update the field, a color scheme containing mappings from all the first 12 ThemeColorTypes to their concrete colors must be provided. Colors for the remaining ThemeColorTypes will be ignored.

---A TextElement kind that represents the beginning of a new paragraph.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.ParagraphMarker
---@field bullet? gcp.slides_v1.Bullet The bullet for this paragraph. If not present, the paragraph does not belong to a list.
---@field style? gcp.slides_v1.ParagraphStyle The paragraph's style

---Styles that apply to a whole paragraph. If this text is contained in a shape with a parent placeholder, then these paragraph styles may be inherited from the parent. Which paragraph styles are inherited depend on the nesting level of lists: * A paragraph not in a list will inherit its paragraph style from the paragraph at the 0 nesting level of the list inside the parent placeholder. * A paragraph in a list will inherit its paragraph style from the paragraph at its corresponding nesting level of the list inside the parent placeholder. Inherited paragraph styles are represented as unset fields in this message.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.ParagraphStyle
---@field spacingMode? gcp.slides_v1.ParagraphStyleSpacingModeEnum|string The spacing mode for the paragraph.
---@field alignment? gcp.slides_v1.ParagraphStyleAlignmentEnum|string The text alignment for this paragraph.
---@field spaceAbove? gcp.slides_v1.Dimension The amount of extra space above the paragraph. If unset, the value is inherited from the parent.
---@field indentStart? gcp.slides_v1.Dimension The amount indentation for the paragraph on the side that corresponds to the start of the text, based on the current text direction. If unset, the value is inherited from the parent.
---@field direction? gcp.slides_v1.ParagraphStyleDirectionEnum|string The text direction of this paragraph. If unset, the value defaults to LEFT_TO_RIGHT since text direction is not inherited.
---@field lineSpacing? number The amount of space between lines, as a percentage of normal, where normal is represented as 100.0. If unset, the value is inherited from the parent.
---@field indentEnd? gcp.slides_v1.Dimension The amount indentation for the paragraph on the side that corresponds to the end of the text, based on the current text direction. If unset, the value is inherited from the parent.
---@field spaceBelow? gcp.slides_v1.Dimension The amount of extra space below the paragraph. If unset, the value is inherited from the parent.
---@field indentFirstLine? gcp.slides_v1.Dimension The amount of indentation for the start of the first line of the paragraph. If unset, the value is inherited from the parent.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.ParagraphStyleAlignmentEnum "ALIGNMENT_UNSPECIFIED"|"START"|"CENTER"|"END"|"JUSTIFIED"

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.ParagraphStyleDirectionEnum "TEXT_DIRECTION_UNSPECIFIED"|"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"|"RIGHT_TO_LEFT"

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.ParagraphStyleSpacingModeEnum "SPACING_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NEVER_COLLAPSE"|"COLLAPSE_LISTS"

---The placeholder information that uniquely identifies a placeholder shape.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.Placeholder
---@field index? number The index of the placeholder. If the same placeholder types are present in the same page, they would have different index values.
---@field type? gcp.slides_v1.PlaceholderTypeEnum|string The type of the placeholder.
---@field parentObjectId? string The object ID of this shape's parent placeholder. If unset, the parent placeholder shape does not exist, so the shape does not inherit properties from any other shape.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.PlaceholderTypeEnum "NONE"|"BODY"|"CHART"|"CLIP_ART"|"CENTERED_TITLE"|"DIAGRAM"|"DATE_AND_TIME"|"FOOTER"|"HEADER"|"MEDIA"|"OBJECT"|"PICTURE"|"SLIDE_NUMBER"|"SUBTITLE"|"TABLE"|"TITLE"|"SLIDE_IMAGE"

---Represents a single post in a comment thread.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.Post
---@field fromCopiedPresentation? boolean Output only. Whether the post is from a copied presentation. This field cannot be set directly by callers.
---@field contentHtml? string Output only. The content of the post as HTML.
---@field fromImportedPresentation? boolean Output only. Whether the post is from an imported presentation. This field cannot be set directly by callers.
---@field assigneeEmail? string Optional. The email of the user who is being newly assigned to the thread as part of this post. Returns a 400 bad request error if: - The parent thread is a CommentThread whose headPost does not have an assignee. - commentAction is specified as `RESOLVE` or `REOPEN`. - `assignee_email` exceeds 2048 UTF-8 code units.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time the post was last updated.
---@field commentAction? gcp.slides_v1.PostCommentActionEnum|string Action taken as part of creating the post.
---@field deleted? boolean Output only. Whether the post is deleted. If `true`, content and author fields will be empty.
---@field author? gcp.slides_v1.PostAuthor Output only. The user who created the post.
---@field content? string The content of the post. Required to be non-empty if comment_action is not `RESOLVE` or `REOPEN`. This text content will be handled similarly to comments created in the Slides editor. It will have similar behaviors for formatting, notifications, etc. May not exceed 2048 UTF-8 code units.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time the post was created.
---@field postId? string Output only. The unique ID of the post.

---Represents a user who authored a comment post.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.PostAuthor
---@field me? boolean Whether the user is the authenticated user making the request.
---@field displayName? string The display name of the user. May be absent if the author is anonymous.
---@field anonymous? boolean Whether the user is anonymous.
---@field user? string The resource name of the post author user, which can also be used to identify the user in the [Google People API](https://developers.google.com/people/api/rest/v1/people). Format: `users/{user}`. Will not be populated if the anonymous field is `true` or if the post is from an imported presentation.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.PostCommentActionEnum "COMMENT_ACTION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NO_COMMENT_ACTION_CHANGE"|"RESOLVE"|"REOPEN"

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.PostList gcp.slides_v1.Post[]

---A Google Slides presentation.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.Presentation
---@field presentationId? string The ID of the presentation.
---@field notesMaster? gcp.slides_v1.Page The notes master in the presentation. It serves three purposes: - Placeholder shapes on a notes master contain the default text styles and shape properties of all placeholder shapes on notes pages. Specifically, a `SLIDE_IMAGE` placeholder shape contains the slide thumbnail, and a `BODY` placeholder shape contains the speaker notes. - The notes master page properties define the common page properties inherited by all notes pages. - Any other shapes on the notes master appear on all notes pages. The notes master is read-only.
---@field layouts? gcp.slides_v1.PageList The layouts in the presentation. A layout is a template that determines how content is arranged and styled on the slides that inherit from that layout.
---@field locale? string The locale of the presentation, as an IETF BCP 47 language tag.
---@field commentsViewMode? gcp.slides_v1.PresentationCommentsViewModeEnum Output only. The comments view mode applied to the presentation.
---@field pageSize? gcp.slides_v1.Size The size of pages in the presentation.
---@field comments? gcp.slides_v1.CommentThreadList Output only. The comment threads associated with the presentation.
---@field slides? gcp.slides_v1.PageList The slides in the presentation. A slide inherits properties from a slide layout.
---@field masters? gcp.slides_v1.PageList The slide masters in the presentation. A slide master contains all common page elements and the common properties for a set of layouts. They serve three purposes: - Placeholder shapes on a master contain the default text styles and shape properties of all placeholder shapes on pages that use that master. - The master page properties define the common page properties inherited by its layouts. - Any other shapes on the master slide appear on all slides using that master, regardless of their layout.
---@field revisionId? string Output only. The revision ID of the presentation. Can be used in update requests to assert the presentation revision hasn't changed since the last read operation. Only populated if the user has edit access to the presentation. The revision ID is not a sequential number but a nebulous string. The format of the revision ID may change over time, so it should be treated opaquely. A returned revision ID is only guaranteed to be valid for 24 hours after it has been returned and cannot be shared across users. If the revision ID is unchanged between calls, then the presentation has not changed. Conversely, a changed ID (for the same presentation and user) usually means the presentation has been updated. However, a changed ID can also be due to internal factors such as ID format changes.
---@field title? string The title of the presentation.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.PresentationCommentsViewModeEnum "COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_DEFAULT_FOR_CURRENT_ACCESS"|"COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_OMITTED"|"COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_INCLUDED"

---Specifies a contiguous range of an indexed collection, such as characters in text.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.Range
---@field endIndex? number The optional zero-based index of the end of the collection. Required for `FIXED_RANGE` ranges.
---@field type? gcp.slides_v1.RangeTypeEnum|string The type of range.
---@field startIndex? number The optional zero-based index of the beginning of the collection. Required for `FIXED_RANGE` and `FROM_START_INDEX` ranges.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.RangeTypeEnum "RANGE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"FIXED_RANGE"|"FROM_START_INDEX"|"ALL"

---A recolor effect applied on an image.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.Recolor
---@field name? gcp.slides_v1.RecolorNameEnum|string The name of the recolor effect. The name is determined from the `recolor_stops` by matching the gradient against the colors in the page's current color scheme. This property is read-only.
---@field recolorStops? gcp.slides_v1.ColorStopList The recolor effect is represented by a gradient, which is a list of color stops. The colors in the gradient will replace the corresponding colors at the same position in the color palette and apply to the image. This property is read-only.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.RecolorNameEnum "NONE"|"LIGHT1"|"LIGHT2"|"LIGHT3"|"LIGHT4"|"LIGHT5"|"LIGHT6"|"LIGHT7"|"LIGHT8"|"LIGHT9"|"LIGHT10"|"DARK1"|"DARK2"|"DARK3"|"DARK4"|"DARK5"|"DARK6"|"DARK7"|"DARK8"|"DARK9"|"DARK10"|"GRAYSCALE"|"NEGATIVE"|"SEPIA"|"CUSTOM"

---Refreshes an embedded Google Sheets chart by replacing it with the latest version of the chart from Google Sheets. NOTE: Refreshing charts requires at least one of the spreadsheets.readonly, spreadsheets, drive.readonly, or drive OAuth scopes.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.RefreshSheetsChartRequest
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the chart to refresh.

---Replaces all shapes that match the given criteria with the provided image. The images replacing the shapes are rectangular after being inserted into the presentation and do not take on the forms of the shapes.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.ReplaceAllShapesWithImageRequest
---@field imageUrl? string The image URL. The image is fetched once at insertion time and a copy is stored for display inside the presentation. Images must be less than 50MB in size, cannot exceed 25 megapixels, and must be in one of PNG, JPEG, or GIF format. The provided URL can be at most 2 kB in length. The URL itself is saved with the image, and exposed via the Image.source_url field.
---@field imageReplaceMethod? gcp.slides_v1.ReplaceAllShapesWithImageRequestImageReplaceMethodEnum|string The image replace method. If you specify both a `replace_method` and an `image_replace_method`, the `image_replace_method` takes precedence. If you do not specify a value for `image_replace_method`, but specify a value for `replace_method`, then the specified `replace_method` value is used. If you do not specify either, then CENTER_INSIDE is used.
---@field containsText? gcp.slides_v1.SubstringMatchCriteria If set, this request will replace all of the shapes that contain the given text.
---@field replaceMethod? gcp.slides_v1.ReplaceAllShapesWithImageRequestReplaceMethodEnum|string The replace method. *Deprecated*: use `image_replace_method` instead. If you specify both a `replace_method` and an `image_replace_method`, the `image_replace_method` takes precedence.
---@field pageObjectIds? gcp.slides_v1.StringList If non-empty, limits the matches to page elements only on the given pages. Returns a 400 bad request error if given the page object ID of a notes page or a notes master, or if a page with that object ID doesn't exist in the presentation.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.ReplaceAllShapesWithImageRequestImageReplaceMethodEnum "IMAGE_REPLACE_METHOD_UNSPECIFIED"|"CENTER_INSIDE"|"CENTER_CROP"

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.ReplaceAllShapesWithImageRequestReplaceMethodEnum "CENTER_INSIDE"|"CENTER_CROP"

---The result of replacing shapes with an image.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.ReplaceAllShapesWithImageResponse
---@field occurrencesChanged? number The number of shapes replaced with images.

---Replaces all shapes that match the given criteria with the provided Google Sheets chart. The chart will be scaled and centered to fit within the bounds of the original shape. NOTE: Replacing shapes with a chart requires at least one of the spreadsheets.readonly, spreadsheets, drive.readonly, or drive OAuth scopes.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.ReplaceAllShapesWithSheetsChartRequest
---@field linkingMode? gcp.slides_v1.ReplaceAllShapesWithSheetsChartRequestLinkingModeEnum|string The mode with which the chart is linked to the source spreadsheet. When not specified, the chart will be an image that is not linked.
---@field spreadsheetId? string The ID of the Google Sheets spreadsheet that contains the chart.
---@field pageObjectIds? gcp.slides_v1.StringList If non-empty, limits the matches to page elements only on the given pages. Returns a 400 bad request error if given the page object ID of a notes page or a notes master, or if a page with that object ID doesn't exist in the presentation.
---@field chartId? number The ID of the specific chart in the Google Sheets spreadsheet.
---@field containsText? gcp.slides_v1.SubstringMatchCriteria The criteria that the shapes must match in order to be replaced. The request will replace all of the shapes that contain the given text.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.ReplaceAllShapesWithSheetsChartRequestLinkingModeEnum "NOT_LINKED_IMAGE"|"LINKED"

---The result of replacing shapes with a Google Sheets chart.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.ReplaceAllShapesWithSheetsChartResponse
---@field occurrencesChanged? number The number of shapes replaced with charts.

---Replaces all instances of text matching a criteria with replace text.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.ReplaceAllTextRequest
---@field pageObjectIds? gcp.slides_v1.StringList If non-empty, limits the matches to page elements only on the given pages. Returns a 400 bad request error if given the page object ID of a notes master, or if a page with that object ID doesn't exist in the presentation.
---@field containsText? gcp.slides_v1.SubstringMatchCriteria Finds text in a shape matching this substring.
---@field replaceText? string The text that will replace the matched text.

---The result of replacing text.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.ReplaceAllTextResponse
---@field occurrencesChanged? number The number of occurrences changed by replacing all text.

---Replaces an existing image with a new image. Replacing an image removes some image effects from the existing image.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.ReplaceImageRequest
---@field imageObjectId? string The ID of the existing image that will be replaced. The ID can be retrieved from the response of a get request.
---@field imageReplaceMethod? gcp.slides_v1.ReplaceImageRequestImageReplaceMethodEnum|string The replacement method.
---@field url? string The image URL. The image is fetched once at insertion time and a copy is stored for display inside the presentation. Images must be less than 50MB, cannot exceed 25 megapixels, and must be in PNG, JPEG, or GIF format. The provided URL can't surpass 2 KB in length. The URL is saved with the image, and exposed through the Image.source_url field.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.ReplaceImageRequestImageReplaceMethodEnum "IMAGE_REPLACE_METHOD_UNSPECIFIED"|"CENTER_INSIDE"|"CENTER_CROP"

---A single kind of update to apply to a presentation.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.Request
