---@field horizontalBorderRows? gcp.slides_v1.TableBorderRowList Properties of horizontal cell borders. A table's horizontal cell borders are represented as a grid. The grid has one more row than the number of rows in the table and the same number of columns as the table. For example, if the table is 3 x 3, its horizontal borders will be represented as a grid with 4 rows and 3 columns.
---@field rows? number Number of rows in the table.
---@field columns? number Number of columns in the table.

