---The general text content. The text must reside in a compatible shape (e.g. text box or rectangle) or a table cell in a page.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.TextContent
---@field textElements? gcp.slides_v1.TextElementList The text contents broken down into its component parts, including styling information. This property is read-only.
---@field lists? gcp.slides_v1.ListMap The bulleted lists contained in this text, keyed by list ID.

---A TextElement describes the content of a range of indices in the text content of a Shape or TableCell.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.TextElement
---@field startIndex? number The zero-based start index of this text element, in Unicode code units.
---@field textRun? gcp.slides_v1.TextRun A TextElement representing a run of text where all of the characters in the run have the same TextStyle. The `start_index` and `end_index` of TextRuns will always be fully contained in the index range of a single `paragraph_marker` TextElement. In other words, a TextRun will never span multiple paragraphs.
---@field paragraphMarker? gcp.slides_v1.ParagraphMarker A marker representing the beginning of a new paragraph. The `start_index` and `end_index` of this TextElement represent the range of the paragraph. Other TextElements with an index range contained inside this paragraph's range are considered to be part of this paragraph. The range of indices of two separate paragraphs will never overlap.
---@field endIndex? number The zero-based end index of this text element, exclusive, in Unicode code units.
---@field autoText? gcp.slides_v1.AutoText A TextElement representing a spot in the text that is dynamically replaced with content that can change over time.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.TextElementList gcp.slides_v1.TextElement[]

---Specifies a contiguous range of text within a shape or table cell's text.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.TextRange
---@field startIndex? number The zero-based index of the beginning range. This field is an Int32Value in order to accommodate future use cases with open-ended ranges.
---@field endIndex? number The zero-based index of the end of the range. This field is an Int32Value in order to accommodate future use cases with open-ended ranges.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.TextRangeList gcp.slides_v1.TextRange[]

---A TextElement kind that represents a run of text that all has the same styling.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.TextRun
---@field content? string The text of this run.
---@field style? gcp.slides_v1.TextStyle The styling applied to this run.

---Represents the styling that can be applied to a TextRun. If this text is contained in a shape with a parent placeholder, then these text styles may be inherited from the parent. Which text styles are inherited depend on the nesting level of lists: * A text run in a paragraph that is not in a list will inherit its text style from the the newline character in the paragraph at the 0 nesting level of the list inside the parent placeholder. * A text run in a paragraph that is in a list will inherit its text style from the newline character in the paragraph at its corresponding nesting level of the list inside the parent placeholder. Inherited text styles are represented as unset fields in this message. If text is contained in a shape without a parent placeholder, unsetting these fields will revert the style to a value matching the defaults in the Slides editor.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.TextStyle
---@field weightedFontFamily? gcp.slides_v1.WeightedFontFamily The font family and rendered weight of the text. This field is an extension of `font_family` meant to support explicit font weights without breaking backwards compatibility. As such, when reading the style of a range of text, the value of `weighted_font_family#font_family` will always be equal to that of `font_family`. However, when writing, if both fields are included in the field mask (either explicitly or through the wildcard `"*"`), their values are reconciled as follows: * If `font_family` is set and `weighted_font_family` is not, the value of `font_family` is applied with weight `400` ("normal"). * If both fields are set, the value of `font_family` must match that of `weighted_font_family#font_family`. If so, the font family and weight of `weighted_font_family` is applied. Otherwise, a 400 bad request error is returned. * If `weighted_font_family` is set and `font_family` is not, the font family and weight of `weighted_font_family` is applied. * If neither field is set, the font family and weight of the text inherit from the parent. Note that these properties cannot inherit separately from each other. If an update request specifies values for both `weighted_font_family` and `bold`, the `weighted_font_family` is applied first, then `bold`. If `weighted_font_family#weight` is not set, it defaults to `400`. If `weighted_font_family` is set, then `weighted_font_family#font_family` must also be set with a non-empty value. Otherwise, a 400 bad request error is returned.
---@field fontFamily? string The font family of the text. The font family can be any font from the Font menu in Slides or from [Google Fonts] (https://fonts.google.com/). If the font name is unrecognized, the text is rendered in `Arial`. Some fonts can affect the weight of the text. If an update request specifies values for both `font_family` and `bold`, the explicitly-set `bold` value is used.
---@field baselineOffset? gcp.slides_v1.TextStyleBaselineOffsetEnum|string The text's vertical offset from its normal position. Text with `SUPERSCRIPT` or `SUBSCRIPT` baseline offsets is automatically rendered in a smaller font size, computed based on the `font_size` field. The `font_size` itself is not affected by changes in this field.
---@field smallCaps? boolean Whether or not the text is in small capital letters.
---@field backgroundColor? gcp.slides_v1.OptionalColor The background color of the text. If set, the color is either opaque or transparent, depending on if the `opaque_color` field in it is set.
---@field foregroundColor? gcp.slides_v1.OptionalColor The color of the text itself. If set, the color is either opaque or transparent, depending on if the `opaque_color` field in it is set.
---@field link? gcp.slides_v1.Link The hyperlink destination of the text. If unset, there is no link. Links are not inherited from parent text. Changing the link in an update request causes some other changes to the text style of the range: * When setting a link, the text foreground color will be set to ThemeColorType.HYPERLINK and the text will be underlined. If these fields are modified in the same request, those values will be used instead of the link defaults. * Setting a link on a text range that overlaps with an existing link will also update the existing link to point to the new URL. * Links are not settable on newline characters. As a result, setting a link on a text range that crosses a paragraph boundary, such as `"ABC\n123"`, will separate the newline character(s) into their own text runs. The link will be applied separately to the runs before and after the newline. * Removing a link will update the text style of the range to match the style of the preceding text (or the default text styles if the preceding text is another link) unless different styles are being set in the same request.
---@field italic? boolean Whether or not the text is italicized.
---@field strikethrough? boolean Whether or not the text is struck through.
---@field fontSize? gcp.slides_v1.Dimension The size of the text's font. When read, the `font_size` will specified in points.
---@field underline? boolean Whether or not the text is underlined.
---@field bold? boolean Whether or not the text is rendered as bold.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.TextStyleBaselineOffsetEnum "BASELINE_OFFSET_UNSPECIFIED"|"NONE"|"SUPERSCRIPT"|"SUBSCRIPT"

---A pair mapping a theme color type to the concrete color it represents.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.ThemeColorPair
---@field type? gcp.slides_v1.ThemeColorPairTypeEnum|string The type of the theme color.
---@field color? gcp.slides_v1.RgbColor The concrete color corresponding to the theme color type above.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.ThemeColorPairList gcp.slides_v1.ThemeColorPair[]

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.ThemeColorPairTypeEnum "THEME_COLOR_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"DARK1"|"LIGHT1"|"DARK2"|"LIGHT2"|"ACCENT1"|"ACCENT2"|"ACCENT3"|"ACCENT4"|"ACCENT5"|"ACCENT6"|"HYPERLINK"|"FOLLOWED_HYPERLINK"|"TEXT1"|"BACKGROUND1"|"TEXT2"|"BACKGROUND2"

---The thumbnail of a page.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.Thumbnail
---@field width? number The positive width in pixels of the thumbnail image.
---@field height? number The positive height in pixels of the thumbnail image.
---@field contentUrl? string The content URL of the thumbnail image. The URL to the image has a default lifetime of 30 minutes. This URL is tagged with the account of the requester. Anyone with the URL effectively accesses the image as the original requester. Access to the image may be lost if the presentation's sharing settings change. The mime type of the thumbnail image is the same as specified in the `GetPageThumbnailRequest`.

---Ungroups objects, such as groups.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.UngroupObjectsRequest
---@field objectIds? gcp.slides_v1.StringList The object IDs of the objects to ungroup. Only groups that are not inside other groups can be ungrouped. All the groups should be on the same page. The group itself is deleted. The visual sizes and positions of all the children are preserved.

---Unmerges cells in a Table.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.UnmergeTableCellsRequest
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the table.
---@field tableRange? gcp.slides_v1.TableRange The table range specifying which cells of the table to unmerge. All merged cells in this range will be unmerged, and cells that are already unmerged will not be affected. If the range has no merged cells, the request will do nothing. If there is text in any of the merged cells, the text will remain in the upper-left ("head") cell of the resulting block of unmerged cells.

---Updates a Post in a CommentThread. Returns a 400 bad request error if: - The requesting user is not the author of the post.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.UpdateCommentPostRequest
---@field content? string The new text of the comment, as plain text. This text content will be handled similarly to comments created in the Slides editor. It will have similar behaviors for formatting, notifications, etc. This field cannot be empty, and must not exceed 2048 UTF-8 code units.
---@field commentId? string The ID of the CommentThread which the post belongs to.
---@field postId? string The ID of the post being updated.

---Update the properties of an Image.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.UpdateImagePropertiesRequest
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the image the updates are applied to.
---@field imageProperties? gcp.slides_v1.ImageProperties The image properties to update.
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root `imageProperties` is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field. For example to update the image outline color, set `fields` to `"outline.outlineFill.solidFill.color"`. To reset a property to its default value, include its field name in the field mask but leave the field itself unset.

---Updates the category of a line.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.UpdateLineCategoryRequest
---@field lineCategory? gcp.slides_v1.UpdateLineCategoryRequestLineCategoryEnum|string The line category to update to. The exact line type is determined based on the category to update to and how it's routed to connect to other page elements.
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the line the update is applied to. Only a line with a category indicating it is a "connector" can be updated. The line may be rerouted after updating its category.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.UpdateLineCategoryRequestLineCategoryEnum "LINE_CATEGORY_UNSPECIFIED"|"STRAIGHT"|"BENT"|"CURVED"

---Updates the properties of a Line.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.UpdateLinePropertiesRequest
---@field lineProperties? gcp.slides_v1.LineProperties The line properties to update.
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the line the update is applied to.
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root `lineProperties` is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field. For example to update the line solid fill color, set `fields` to `"lineFill.solidFill.color"`. To reset a property to its default value, include its field name in the field mask but leave the field itself unset.

---Updates the alt text title and/or description of a page element.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.UpdatePageElementAltTextRequest
---@field description? string The updated alt text description of the page element. If unset the existing value will be maintained. The description is exposed to screen readers and other accessibility interfaces. Only use human readable values related to the content of the page element.
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the page element the updates are applied to.
---@field title? string The updated alt text title of the page element. If unset the existing value will be maintained. The title is exposed to screen readers and other accessibility interfaces. Only use human readable values related to the content of the page element.

---Updates the transform of a page element. Updating the transform of a group will change the absolute transform of the page elements in that group, which can change their visual appearance. See the documentation for PageElement.transform for more details.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.UpdatePageElementTransformRequest
---@field transform? gcp.slides_v1.AffineTransform The input transform matrix used to update the page element.
---@field applyMode? gcp.slides_v1.UpdatePageElementTransformRequestApplyModeEnum|string The apply mode of the transform update.
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the page element to update.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.UpdatePageElementTransformRequestApplyModeEnum "APPLY_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"RELATIVE"|"ABSOLUTE"

---Updates the Z-order of page elements. Z-order is an ordering of the elements on the page from back to front. The page element in the front may cover the elements that are behind it.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.UpdatePageElementsZOrderRequest
---@field operation? gcp.slides_v1.UpdatePageElementsZOrderRequestOperationEnum|string The Z-order operation to apply on the page elements. When applying the operation on multiple page elements, the relative Z-orders within these page elements before the operation is maintained.
---@field pageElementObjectIds? gcp.slides_v1.StringList The object IDs of the page elements to update. All the page elements must be on the same page and must not be grouped.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.UpdatePageElementsZOrderRequestOperationEnum "Z_ORDER_OPERATION_UNSPECIFIED"|"BRING_TO_FRONT"|"BRING_FORWARD"|"SEND_BACKWARD"|"SEND_TO_BACK"

---Updates the properties of a Page.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.UpdatePagePropertiesRequest
---@field pageProperties? gcp.slides_v1.PageProperties The page properties to update.
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the page the update is applied to.
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root `pageProperties` is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field. For example to update the page background solid fill color, set `fields` to `"pageBackgroundFill.solidFill.color"`. To reset a property to its default value, include its field name in the field mask but leave the field itself unset.

---Updates the styling for all of the paragraphs within a Shape or Table that overlap with the given text index range.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.UpdateParagraphStyleRequest
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root `style` is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field. For example, to update the paragraph alignment, set `fields` to `"alignment"`. To reset a property to its default value, include its field name in the field mask but leave the field itself unset.
---@field textRange? gcp.slides_v1.Range The range of text containing the paragraph(s) to style.
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the shape or table with the text to be styled.
---@field style? gcp.slides_v1.ParagraphStyle The paragraph's style.
---@field cellLocation? gcp.slides_v1.TableCellLocation The location of the cell in the table containing the paragraph(s) to style. If `object_id` refers to a table, `cell_location` must have a value. Otherwise, it must not.

---Update the properties of a Shape.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.UpdateShapePropertiesRequest
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root `shapeProperties` is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field. For example to update the shape background solid fill color, set `fields` to `"shapeBackgroundFill.solidFill.color"`. To reset a property to its default value, include its field name in the field mask but leave the field itself unset.
---@field shapeProperties? gcp.slides_v1.ShapeProperties The shape properties to update.
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the shape the updates are applied to.

---Updates the properties of a Slide.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.UpdateSlidePropertiesRequest
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the slide the update is applied to.
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root 'slideProperties' is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field. For example to update whether a slide is skipped, set `fields` to `"isSkipped"`. To reset a property to its default value, include its field name in the field mask but leave the field itself unset.
---@field slideProperties? gcp.slides_v1.SlideProperties The slide properties to update.

---Updates the position of slides in the presentation.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.UpdateSlidesPositionRequest
---@field slideObjectIds? gcp.slides_v1.StringList The IDs of the slides in the presentation that should be moved. The slides in this list must be in existing presentation order, without duplicates.
---@field insertionIndex? number The index where the slides should be inserted, based on the slide arrangement before the move takes place. Must be between zero and the number of slides in the presentation, inclusive.

---Updates the properties of the table borders in a Table.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.UpdateTableBorderPropertiesRequest
---@field tableBorderProperties? gcp.slides_v1.TableBorderProperties The table border properties to update.
---@field tableRange? gcp.slides_v1.TableRange The table range representing the subset of the table to which the updates are applied. If a table range is not specified, the updates will apply to the entire table.
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the table.
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root `tableBorderProperties` is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field. For example to update the table border solid fill color, set `fields` to `"tableBorderFill.solidFill.color"`. To reset a property to its default value, include its field name in the field mask but leave the field itself unset.
---@field borderPosition? gcp.slides_v1.UpdateTableBorderPropertiesRequestBorderPositionEnum|string The border position in the table range the updates should apply to. If a border position is not specified, the updates will apply to all borders in the table range.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.UpdateTableBorderPropertiesRequestBorderPositionEnum "ALL"|"BOTTOM"|"INNER"|"INNER_HORIZONTAL"|"INNER_VERTICAL"|"LEFT"|"OUTER"|"RIGHT"|"TOP"

---Update the properties of a TableCell.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.UpdateTableCellPropertiesRequest
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root `tableCellProperties` is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field. For example to update the table cell background solid fill color, set `fields` to `"tableCellBackgroundFill.solidFill.color"`. To reset a property to its default value, include its field name in the field mask but leave the field itself unset.
---@field tableRange? gcp.slides_v1.TableRange The table range representing the subset of the table to which the updates are applied. If a table range is not specified, the updates will apply to the entire table.
---@field tableCellProperties? gcp.slides_v1.TableCellProperties The table cell properties to update.
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the table.

---Updates the properties of a Table column.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.UpdateTableColumnPropertiesRequest
---@field columnIndices? gcp.slides_v1.IntegerList The list of zero-based indices specifying which columns to update. If no indices are provided, all columns in the table will be updated.
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root `tableColumnProperties` is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field. For example to update the column width, set `fields` to `"column_width"`. If '"column_width"' is included in the field mask but the property is left unset, the column width will default to 406,400 EMU (32 points).
---@field tableColumnProperties? gcp.slides_v1.TableColumnProperties The table column properties to update. If the value of `table_column_properties#column_width` in the request is less than 406,400 EMU (32 points), a 400 bad request error is returned.
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the table.

---Updates the properties of a Table row.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.UpdateTableRowPropertiesRequest
---@field rowIndices? gcp.slides_v1.IntegerList The list of zero-based indices specifying which rows to update. If no indices are provided, all rows in the table will be updated.
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the table.
---@field tableRowProperties? gcp.slides_v1.TableRowProperties The table row properties to update.
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root `tableRowProperties` is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field. For example to update the minimum row height, set `fields` to `"min_row_height"`. If '"min_row_height"' is included in the field mask but the property is left unset, the minimum row height will default to 0.

---Update the styling of text in a Shape or Table.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.UpdateTextStyleRequest
---@field style? gcp.slides_v1.TextStyle The style(s) to set on the text. If the value for a particular style matches that of the parent, that style will be set to inherit. Certain text style changes may cause other changes meant to mirror the behavior of the Slides editor. See the documentation of TextStyle for more information.
---@field cellLocation? gcp.slides_v1.TableCellLocation The location of the cell in the table containing the text to style. If `object_id` refers to a table, `cell_location` must have a value. Otherwise, it must not.
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root `style` is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field. For example, to update the text style to bold, set `fields` to `"bold"`. To reset a property to its default value, include its field name in the field mask but leave the field itself unset.
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the shape or table with the text to be styled.
---@field textRange? gcp.slides_v1.Range The range of text to style. The range may be extended to include adjacent newlines. If the range fully contains a paragraph belonging to a list, the paragraph's bullet is also updated with the matching text style.

---Update the properties of a Video.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.UpdateVideoPropertiesRequest
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root `videoProperties` is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field. For example to update the video outline color, set `fields` to `"outline.outlineFill.solidFill.color"`. To reset a property to its default value, include its field name in the field mask but leave the field itself unset.
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the video the updates are applied to.
---@field videoProperties? gcp.slides_v1.VideoProperties The video properties to update.

---A PageElement kind representing a video.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.Video
---@field url? string An URL to a video. The URL is valid as long as the source video exists and sharing settings do not change.
---@field id? string The video source's unique identifier for this video.
---@field source? gcp.slides_v1.VideoSourceEnum|string The video source.
---@field videoProperties? gcp.slides_v1.VideoProperties The properties of the video.

---The properties of the Video.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.VideoProperties
---@field outline? gcp.slides_v1.Outline The outline of the video. The default outline matches the defaults for new videos created in the Slides editor.
---@field ["end"]? number The time at which to end playback, measured in seconds from the beginning of the video. If set, the end time should be after the start time. If not set or if you set this to a value that exceeds the video's length, the video will be played until its end.
---@field start? number The time at which to start playback, measured in seconds from the beginning of the video. If set, the start time should be before the end time. If you set this to a value that exceeds the video's length in seconds, the video will be played from the last second. If not set, the video will be played from the beginning.
---@field mute? boolean Whether to mute the audio during video playback. Defaults to false.
---@field autoPlay? boolean Whether to enable video autoplay when the page is displayed in present mode. Defaults to false.

---@alias gcp.slides_v1.VideoSourceEnum "SOURCE_UNSPECIFIED"|"YOUTUBE"|"DRIVE"

---Represents a font family and weight used to style a TextRun.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.WeightedFontFamily
---@field fontFamily? string The font family of the text. The font family can be any font from the Font menu in Slides or from [Google Fonts] (https://fonts.google.com/). If the font name is unrecognized, the text is rendered in `Arial`.
---@field weight? number The rendered weight of the text. This field can have any value that is a multiple of `100` between `100` and `900`, inclusive. This range corresponds to the numerical values described in the CSS 2.1 Specification, [section 15.6](https://www.w3.org/TR/CSS21/fonts.html#font-boldness), with non-numerical values disallowed. Weights greater than or equal to `700` are considered bold, and weights less than `700`are not bold. The default value is `400` ("normal").

---A PageElement kind representing word art.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.WordArt
---@field renderedText? string The text rendered as word art.

---Provides control over how write requests are executed.
---@class gcp.slides_v1.WriteControl
---@field requiredRevisionId? string The revision ID of the presentation required for the write request. If specified and the required revision ID doesn't match the presentation's current revision ID, the request is not processed and returns a 400 bad request error. When a required revision ID is returned in a response, it indicates the revision ID of the document after the request was applied.

---@class gcp.slides_v1.BadRequestError: distilled.Error
---@field tag "BadRequest"

---@class gcp.slides_v1.ConflictError: distilled.Error
---@field tag "Conflict"

---@class gcp.slides_v1.ForbiddenError: distilled.Error
---@field tag "Forbidden"

---@class gcp.slides_v1.NotFoundError: distilled.Error
---@field tag "NotFound"

---@class gcp.slides_v1.Options
---@field access_token? string|distilled.Secret|fun(host: table): (string|distilled.Secret|nil, distilled.Error?)
---@field credentials? table
---@field endpoint? string
---@field quota_project? string
---@field regional_endpoints? string
---@field host? table The host seams: transport, sleep, now, exec, random, getenv, epoch
---@field transport? fun(request: table): (table?, distilled.Error?)
---@field sleep? fun(seconds: number)
---@field now? fun(): number
---@field retry? string|table A retry preset or policy fields
---@field deadline_s? number Wall-clock budget for one call, sleeps included
---@field tracing? "off"|"operation"|"debug"|table
---@field validation? "lenient"|"additional"|"strict"
---@field [string] any

---@class gcp.slides_v1.Module
local Module = {}

---@param options? gcp.slides_v1.Options
